# Deploy Workflow

## Direct-to-master

When yui direct mei to make changes, mei should:

1. Work on `master` directly -- no feature branches, no PRs.
2. Commit with clear messages (still multiple small commits, not one blob).
3. Push to `master`, which triggers the deploy pipeline to the live site.

If the cloud agent system assigns a feature branch, override it: check out `master`, make changes there, push to `master`. The PR-review ceremony is unnecessary for this project -- yui trust mei to push working code.

## When a PR branch has already been created

If mei have already committed to a feature branch before seeing this rule, merge it into `master` and push `master`. Clean up the feature branch.

## Exceptions

- If yui explicitly ask for a PR or branch, do that instead.
- If mei are genuinely uncertain about a change, ask before pushing to master.

## Version + deploy (what yui actually needs)

Two goals only:

1. **New code reaches the live site.** A change that affects served files must
   land on `master` (direct push or merged PR). That triggers GitHub Actions →
   rsync → https://fuseki.net/music8899b/. Reload the page to see it.
2. **Yui can tell which build is loaded.** The header version label and every
   asset `?v=N` are the same number from `VERSION` / `app-version.js`. After a
   deploy, reload and check the header: if it shows the version just shipped,
   the browser has the new build; if not, hard-reload or wait for the Action.

### When to bump

Run `./bump-version.sh` **once per ship**, in the **same push** as the
user-facing change. Never push a bump-only commit (it burns a deploy and
races other agents). Never bump after a successful push "to open the next
cycle" — the next ship bumps when it ships.

```
work, commit…  →  ./bump-version.sh  →  commit version files with the change  →  push master once  →  deploy live as vN
                                                                                                      →  reload; header shows vN
```

### When not to bump

Skip the bump when the push touches only files rsync excludes (docs `*.md`,
tests, `.cursor/`, scripts, etc.). Those never reach the server, so a new
`?v=` does nothing for visitors.

### Concurrent agents

Before the ship push: `git fetch origin master` and rebase (or reset+cherry-pick
onto origin). If `VERSION` moved, re-run `./bump-version.sh` so the ship is
exactly one past origin, then push once with content + version together.
